WEBVTT

00:00:29.579 --> 00:00:31.204
However, when stress is permanent,

00:00:31.246 --> 00:00:33.704
such as the stress
most of us experience each day,

00:00:33.746 --> 00:00:36.954
it actually starts to change your brain.

00:00:37.454 --> 00:00:38.662
Chronic stress,

00:00:38.704 --> 00:00:42.037
when we are overburdened at work
or we argue at home,

00:00:42.121 --> 00:00:43.746
can affect the size of your brain,

00:00:43.787 --> 00:00:47.704
its structure, the way it works,
down to the level of your genes.

00:00:48.246 --> 00:00:50.204
Stress begins with what is called

00:00:50.246 --> 00:00:52.954
the “Hypothalamic-Pituitary-Adrenal axis”,

00:00:52.996 --> 00:00:57.454
a series of interactions of the endocrine 
glands in the brain and kidney,

00:00:57.496 --> 00:01:00.621
that controls your body’s 
response to stress.